sbe1v1k: dts: run the fan PWM at 1 kHz (test)

The fan is a Delta ASB0512HA. On the OpenWrt forum (thread 245244,
posts 45, 51 and 53, motolav, February 2026) it ran best at a 1 kHz
PWM: quiet and usable over the whole duty range, while 5-10 kHz only
spun it weakly and 2.5 kHz was noisy. Delta specifies a 1 kHz PWM for
similar fans (THA series). The device tree has used 40000 ns (25 kHz)
since the board was added.

Caveat: those measurements predate qualcommbe 0403 ("pwm: fix period
calculation", June 2026). Before it, pwm-ipq could not produce periods
shorter than (pwm_div + 1) / clk and scaled the duty cycle wrongly, so
the poor results above 1 kHz were at least partly the driver. With
0403 both periods are exact at the 100 MHz ADSS PWM clock: 25 kHz is
pre_div 0 / pwm_div 3999, 1 kHz is pre_div 1 / pwm_div 49999 (finer
duty steps). This is a test item to compare by ear and by temperature
against 25 kHz; drop the patch to go back.

The cooling levels (36/72/128/255) and trip points are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
index caa5cf24c6..50ac381ea9 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -114,7 +114,11 @@
 
 	fan: pwm-fan {
 		compatible = "pwm-fan";
-		pwms = <&pwm 3 40000 0>;
+		/*
+		 * 1 kHz rather than the 25 kHz of PC fans: the Delta
+		 * ASB0512HA runs quietly over its whole range at 1 kHz.
+		 */
+		pwms = <&pwm 3 1000000 0>;
 		#cooling-cells = <2>;
 		cooling-levels = <36 72 128 255>;
 	};
